{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1019406,"ns":0,"title":"Cuthill–McKee algorithm","extract":"In numerical linear algebra, the Cuthill–McKee algorithm (CM), named after Elizabeth Cuthill and James McKee, is an algorithm to permute a sparse matrix that has a symmetric sparsity pattern into a   band matrix form with a small bandwidth. The reverse Cuthill–McKee algorithm  (RCM)  due to Alan George and Joseph Liu is the same algorithm but with the resulting index numbers reversed.","description":"Numerical linear algebra algorithm","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}